WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.242 --> 00:00:01.990
(upbeat music playing)

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:03.320
A lot of work goes into a short,

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.770
late night stand-up set.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.390
Join me J.P. Buck, as I
spotlight the comedians

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.900
who came up with some of
my favorite CONAN sets.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.733
This is, The Set Up.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.194
[Conan] Please welcome the
very funny Daniel Sloss!

00:00:16.194 --> 00:00:18.810
(upbeat music playing)

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.310
I remember, well, to be fair,

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.930
I think in your head you were like,

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.082
right, we're gonna do the set,

00:00:23.082 --> 00:00:24.030
we're gonna do it on television.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:27.310
I never believed I was
going to be on CONAN

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:29.840
until the curtains pulled back.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.806
And it wasn't until I physically was there

00:00:31.806 --> 00:00:32.639
and I heard it like,

00:00:32.639 --> 00:00:33.640
that was the moment where I was like,

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.250
oh okay, now they're not
gonna take it away from you.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:39.010
So when I went, when we
were talking about my set,

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.850
when we were booking and
we were organizing dates,

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.840
the entire time I was
like this isn't happening.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.240
Something will happen, they like I,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.270
something else will come up

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.790
or they'll realize their mistake.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:49.600
And then we start getting on
the plane on the way there,

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.433
now I was excited,

00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:52.800
I'm like this feels like
it might be happening.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:53.890
And then I got to the hotel,

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.420
and it was like the day of the recording,

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.420
and we go along to the studios
and it's all very exciting.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:00:59.820
And I don't know if you remember this,

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.720
but I'm just like oh my
god, I might actually,

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.420
this might be the time I
get to perform on CONAN.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.913
And then Nelson Mandela died.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.590
It was the day Nelson Mandela died.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.950
Because I remembered, how
selfish I am as a human being.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.750
One of the greatest men
who has ever lived died

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.290
and my first reaction was,

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.890
I bet I don't get to be on CONAN anymore.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.802
Like that's, it's too sad,
they'll pull tonight's show,

00:01:21.802 --> 00:01:23.213
I'm not going to get the moment.

00:01:23.213 --> 00:01:26.760
I know, I know. I understand
now what I was doing,

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.960
but at the time, I just,

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.160
Well, what's worse, losing that spot,

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:32.570
because of Nelson Mandela dying

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:36.210
or actually having to go out and be funny

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.810
the day of his passing?

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:39.410
Yeah.
What's worse?

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:40.870
Well, I mean,

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.300
oh, you know, when you put it
that way, now I look worse,

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.620
now it looks worse that I did it.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:45.960
Knowing that while everyone was,

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.023
while everyone was mourning,
I was like, hold on, hold on,

00:01:49.023 --> 00:01:51.800
hold on, everyone, everyone,
let's not remember him,

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.410
let's get back to
straight white men, okay?

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.230
Please, back here, all eyes
back to me, come on now.

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:59.820
Possibly the whitest
comedian we could book.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:00.653
Yeah.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.570
That was, that was, I
mean, it looks bad on us,

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.200
it's like, this is our response,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.510
our response to Nelson Mandela passing is,

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.330
here, here's the whitest
comedian we can find.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:11.149
Yeah, and then, and then Jim Gaffigan.

00:02:11.149 --> 00:02:12.740
(upbeat music playing)

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:14.410
There's a joke that was
supposed to be in the set

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.800
right after this.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.900
That was the one that I told you,

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.490
I don't think it's gonna go over well,

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.540
I don't think it's, the
audience is gonna love it,

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.840
why don't we just cut it?

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:24.078
Yeah.

00:02:24.078 --> 00:02:27.480
Which was the obesity versus gay joke.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.590
Oh yes, yes, we did that on, and you were,

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:33.170
you were absolutely right to
make that call, because when I,

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.110
I don't know because, you, I
mean, I told you, I was like,

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:38.600
I don't think you should do
this and you pulled it out,

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.370
but then you put it in the set that,

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.670
you came back two months
later on the show,

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.123
and you did the joke there,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.320
and it got an applause break.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:50.530
A country that believes
that obesity is a disease,

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:53.899
but homosexuality is a choice.

00:02:53.899 --> 00:02:55.670
(audience laughing)

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:56.960
Okay, so if you're fat,

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.730
don't worry about it
that's not your fault,

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.860
you were probably born that
way, but if you're gay,

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.154
must be something you ate.

00:03:02.154 --> 00:03:04.410
(audience laughing)

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.092
Was it penis?

00:03:06.092 --> 00:03:09.092
(audience laughing)

00:03:10.144 --> 00:03:13.144
(audience clapping)

00:03:15.247 --> 00:03:16.988
Maybe I just don't know what I'm doing.

00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:18.700
I mean, that's absolutely not the case,

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.830
but sure, that's much better,

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.410
that's much better than
me self-reflecting,

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.308
so let's go for that one yes.

00:03:23.308 --> 00:03:25.975
(J.P. laughing)

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:28.810
I'm a terrible boyfriend, like,

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:29.680
you always have to do the things

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.440
when you're in a
relationship, for example,

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.500
telling a girl that she's
the most beautiful girl

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.333
in the world.

00:03:34.333 --> 00:03:35.660
I never told my ex-girlfriend

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.550
that she was the most
beautiful girl in the world.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.720
And that was for personal reasons.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.226
It's cause she wasn't.

00:03:41.226 --> 00:03:42.380
(audience laughing)

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.940
Not in a bad way.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:46.290
She was very good
looking, but my logic is,

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:49.820
there are 3.5 billion

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.980
women on earth,

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:56.020
there can be only one, most
beautiful girl in the world,

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:59.073
that's how it works,
that's what that means.

00:03:59.073 --> 00:04:00.000
(audience laughing)

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.272
so, all I'm saying is that, statistically,

00:04:03.272 --> 00:04:05.070
(audience laughing)

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:06.730
probably wasn't her.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:07.700
Has statistics ever

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.260
helped you win an argument
in a relationship?

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.660
No, no, it's,

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:13.070
not in a relationship, cause,

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:15.250
relationship arguments are
never about statistics,

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.391
deep down.

00:04:16.391 --> 00:04:17.990
(both laughing)

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.850
you learn, now that I
am in a relationship,

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.070
you learn that it's not about being right,

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.010
it's about being happy.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.610
There are a lot of jokes that,

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.090
that's like the biggest,

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.430
the biggest reaction to me
may come at a punchline.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:33.120
And then the tags, kind
of peter off a little bit.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.427
For me, this joke kinda goes
here, and then you tag it,

00:04:37.427 --> 00:04:41.240
and that tag for me, is
what is the crescendo.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.930
Oh the tag coming up?

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:43.840
Yeah.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.850
There can only be one, most
beautiful girl in the world.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.838
That's how it works,
that's what that means.

00:04:50.838 --> 00:04:51.810
(audience laughing)

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:55.017
so, all I'm saying is that, statistically,

00:04:55.017 --> 00:04:56.920
(audience laughing)

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:59.018
probably wasn't her, okay.

00:04:59.018 --> 00:04:59.851
(audience laughing)

00:04:59.851 --> 00:05:01.410
She was livid, right?

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:04.836
She stormed out halfway
through my PowerPoint, right.

00:05:04.836 --> 00:05:08.410
Just left, crying and phoning her mom,

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.788
Just because you paint
a ridiculous scenario,

00:05:10.788 --> 00:05:11.930
(both laughing)

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:13.548
you reveal that this
argument is now taking place

00:05:13.548 --> 00:05:15.380
at like a lecture hall.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.640
Yeah, yeah. It goes from, like,

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.090
they're slightly on my side

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:23.740
because they can follow my
twisted mathematical logic of it,

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:27.100
and then you pan out to
reveal the scene of it,

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.130
they weren't imagining it,

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:30.900
this is literally how I'm
explaining it to my girlfriend,

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.173
I am a nightmare.

